<title>FRANCE: Algeria insurance firm posts $5.8 million profit.</title>
<headline>Algeria insurance firm posts $5.8 million profit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's state-owned insurance company, Societe Nationale d'Assurance (SAA), made 323.3 million dinars ($5.8 million) net profit in 1995, the official Algerian news agency APS said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The SAA, which gave the data following the meeting of its board in December, had a turnover of 13.9 billion dinars ($248.2 million) in 1995, APS said.</p>
<p>APS did not give 1996 results. ($1 = 56 dinars)</p>
</text>
